{"body":"The separated-verb gate only accepts articles and pronouns as object heads, while the neighboring determiner list already recognizes quantifiers such as `each`, `every`, `some`, and `no`. Valid plain-language queries such as `logs every user in` or `sign some requests in` therefore never add `login`/`signin`, because `searchCompoundObjectHeads` rejects the object before the format-preposition guard runs. Include common quantifier determiners (while retaining the format guard) or broaden this object-head check.","commit_id":"f52f6088ebbf4da6163627999fc70381794890b1","html_url":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/248#discussion_r3986270733","id":3986270733,"line":4944,"original_line":4944,"path":"internal/sem/search.go","pull_request_review_id":5175343167,"user":"Copilot"}
{"body":"Adding aliases to `q.terms` also sends them through `symbolSearchScore`, whose name path still uses raw `strings.Contains` (search.go:5785-5787). A prose query for `integer` therefore adds `int` and gives symbols such as `Interface`, `Internal`, and `Print` a symbol-name bonus, even though the new token-scoped abbreviation test explicitly rejects those substring matches. Make inferred aliases boundary-aware in every scoring path (or keep them out of substring symbol scoring), otherwise retrieval reintroduces the false positives this change is intended to avoid.","commit_id":"f52f6088ebbf4da6163627999fc70381794890b1","html_url":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/248#discussion_r3986270746","id":3986270746,"line":5172,"original_line":5172,"path":"internal/sem/search.go","pull_request_review_id":5175343167,"user":"Copilot"}
{"body":"This fixture is supposed to ensure that the `authentication` case can reach `auth.go` only through the alias table, but the raw string itself contains `\"authentication\"` and `\"authenticate\"` in its comments. Search indexes documentation, so removing the alias table would still retrieve this file and the eval would not catch a broken alias-retrieval implementation. Keep the long-form query spellings out of the fixture comments and body.","commit_id":"f52f6088ebbf4da6163627999fc70381794890b1","html_url":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/248#discussion_r3986270773","id":3986270773,"line":65,"original_line":65,"path":"internal/sem/search_eval_test.go","pull_request_review_id":5175343167,"user":"Copilot"}
{"body":"The configuration fixtures have the same leakage: this comment contains the literal `configuration` term. Because comments are indexed, both the `configuration` case and the plural case (which derives the singular) can retrieve `config.go` without abbreviation expansion, so these eval cases do not verify alias retrieval. Remove the long-form spelling from the fixture text.","commit_id":"f52f6088ebbf4da6163627999fc70381794890b1","html_url":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/248#discussion_r3986270791","id":3986270791,"line":118,"original_line":118,"path":"internal/sem/search_eval_test.go","pull_request_review_id":5175343167,"user":"Copilot"}

