{"body":"The boundary filter runs only after the Aho scan has used `remaining` to stop. For an inferred alias such as `int`, text like `print(); readInt()` sets `found` on the substring in `print`, exits before reaching `readInt`, and this block then clears the false hit without rescanning, so the valid later alias is lost from retrieval. Validate alias boundaries before decrementing `remaining`, or rescan when a filtered hit is rejected.","html_url":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/248#discussion_r3986364160","id":3986364160,"line":134,"path":"internal/sem/search_matcher.go"}
{"body":"Adding aliases to `q.terms` does not make BM25 count aliases embedded in code identifiers: `searchTermCounts` still increments only for exact token equality. A hit such as `runAuthenticated` can pass the alias-aware retrieval matcher but contribute no `auth` frequency; if that is the only hit in a region, `makeSearchCandidate` drops it when `len(counts) == 0`, so the claimed scoring/BM25 path never returns it. Make term counting use the same alias-aware token logic (and keep the sparse path consistent).","html_url":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/248#discussion_r3986364185","id":3986364185,"line":5233,"path":"internal/sem/search.go"}
{"body":"These aliases are added with weight 0.55, so `searchGitGrepPreselectionPatterns` classifies them as derived and retains only `derived[0]`. A query such as `authentication configuration` can therefore grep for one alias but omit the other; once any term produces a non-empty match set, files containing only the omitted alias are never scanned on large worktrees. Preserve all alias patterns or add a fallback/widening pass for them so alias expansion does not still lose whole code clusters.","html_url":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/248#discussion_r3986364206","id":3986364206,"line":5233,"path":"internal/sem/search.go"}

